course: dictionary
lesson: 5294
title: Jurassic: a time, a thing, and a joke
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a time in history. Read the words around it for clues. «Earth's history is divided into eons, eras and periods, such as the Jurassic, about 200 to 145 million years ago, and the Cretaceous.» The years tell you that the Jurassic is a long time ago, so it must be a period of history.
explain: When Jurassic describes something, it means it comes from that time. «Jurassic rocks» and «Jurassic fossils» are rocks and fossils from millions of years ago. Check by swapping in a meaning: «fossils from the time of the dinosaurs» still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Jurassic also has a capital J in names. The film «Jurassic Park» is a title, not a time. Some people also use Jurassic as a joke. If someone says «Dad's phone is positively Jurassic», they mean it is very old-fashioned. Ask yourself: is this a time, a description, or a joke? The sentence will tell you.
fact: The Jurassic is a long period of Earth's history, about 200 to 145 million years ago, in the middle of the age of dinosaurs.
fact: It comes between the Triassic and the Cretaceous. Dinosaurs such as Stegosaurus and Brachiosaurus lived then, and so did the first birds.
fact: The Jurassic Coast in Dorset and Devon is full of fossils, and Mary Anning searched for them there.
fact: T. rex lived later, in the Cretaceous, so it was not a Jurassic dinosaur, even though the film is called «Jurassic Park».
fact: «Jurassic» can be used as a joke to mean very old-fashioned.
exercise: Which period comes right before the Jurassic in Earth's history? | Ice Age | *Triassic | Cretaceous | Victorian
exercise: In «Dad's phone is positively Jurassic», what does Jurassic mean? | Made of dinosaur bones | Very fast | *Very old-fashioned, as a joke | Brand new and shiny
exercise: Where did Mary Anning search for fossils? | The Scottish Highlands | The Sahara Desert | *The Jurassic Coast | The Amazon rainforest
test: Which dinosaur lived in the Jurassic? | T. rex | *Stegosaurus | Woolly mammoth
test: In «Earth's history is divided into eons, eras and periods, such as the Jurassic, about 200 to 145 million years ago», what clue shows the Jurassic is a time? | The word such as | The word divided | The word eons | *The years given: about 200 to 145 million years ago
exam: Which best describes the Jurassic as a time? | *A long period of Earth's history, in the age of dinosaurs | A small town in Dorset | A kind of mosquito | A type of petrol station
